        {
          "kicker": "Coaching appointment",
          "heading": "Jake White named Fiji head coach, replacing interim Senirusi Seruvakula",
          "body": "Jake White's appointment as Fiji head coach, made last week, hands him a side ranked 10th in the world that has lost four of five Tests this year. He replaces interim coach Senirusi Seruvakula after a field of 31 applicants, and Fiji face Japan this weekend before Nations Championship games against France, Ireland and Italy in November. Former Bulls backline coach Chris Rossouw says he would not be surprised if Fiji surprise people, while Willem Strauss said: \"I think Fiji needs its South African discipline.\""
