      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Autumn warning",
          "heading": "Dan Cole fears Prem's attacking style leaves England exposed against Australia",
          "body": "Former England prop Dan Cole has admitted he is anxious that the Prem's attacking emphasis is leaving England's players short of Test rugby. Speaking on the For the Love of Rugby podcast, Cole said the league's style does not translate to international rugby, citing the attritional, breakdown-heavy nature of recent Tests. With Steve Borthwick's side due to face Australia at Twickenham, Cole's concern is that England go into the autumn without Test-match rugby behind them."
        },
