      "edition": "Tuesday 20 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "WXV rout",
          "heading": "Desiree Miller scores twice as women's Wallaroos thrash Scotland 56-12 in Sydney",
          "body": "Australia's women's side, the Wallaroos, ran in eight tries in a 56-12 WXV Global Series win over Scotland in Sydney, leading 35-5 at the break. Desiree Miller and Amelia Whitaker both scored twice, with Brittany Merlo, Maya Stewart, Ellis and Eva Karpani also crossing. Scotland, under caretaker head coach Dave Butcher, lost Sarah Bonar to illness shortly before kick-off, and have now lost eight straight, four of them in the new competition."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "All Blacks' Ardie Savea and Ruben Love miss end-of-year tour",
