    "463": {
      "date": "2026-10-20",
      "edition": "Tuesday 20 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Sevens title",
          "heading": "Japan women's sevens retain Asia Rugby title with undefeated campaign in Colombo",
          "body": "Japan's women's sevens side beat China 14-7 in the Colombo final to defend the Asia Rugby Emirates Sevens Series title, finishing undefeated across the leg. The Sakura Sevens, who finished with the maximum 40 series points, head to HSBC SVNS, where Japan are already competing. Head coach Yuka Kanematsu said she was \"truly proud\" of the players, five of them making debuts. The men's side also won Leg 2, beating Hong Kong China 28-14 in the final, but Hong Kong China kept the series on points difference."
